  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The smaller the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pKa</mi></math>, the stronger the acid. The acidic nature of the compound depends on the stability of conjugate base.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\ot3_0194_a210c2442b59.png\" style=\"width: 219px; height: 144px;\" /></p><p>The stability of conjugate base formed by above compound is more stable than other three compounds given.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0194_0cd0da695ac4.png\" style=\"width: 328px; height: 114px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0194_9b3d35fdc5cf.png\" style=\"width: 360px; height: 125px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0194_4bd961c405d8.png\" style=\"width: 464px; height: 149px;\" /></p><p>So it has least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pKa</mi></math> value.</p></blockquote>"
